+
+{ch:'traps',type:'wr',
+ q:'Across the visual tests, what is the rule about waiting for the GUI, and which two qtbot helpers are used instead of sleeping? Name where each is used.',
+ concepts:[
+   {label:'never time.sleep',terms:['never sleep','no sleep','not time.sleep','avoid sleep']},
+   {label:'qtbot.waitUntil for the block to appear',terms:['waituntil','wait_until','waitUntil','blocks == 1']},
+   {label:'qtbot.waitExposed for the window',terms:['waitexposed','wait_exposed','waitExposed','exposed']},
+   {label:'processEvents flushes paint events',terms:['processevents','process_events','processEvents','flush']},
+ ],
+ model:'Rule: never use time.sleep to wait for the GUI — it is either too short (flaky) or too slow. Use qtbot.waitExposed(window, timeout=5000) to wait until a window is actually shown (main window / canvas tests), and qtbot.waitUntil(lambda: len(window.canvas.blocks) == 1, timeout=...) to wait until an interaction (clicking the toolbar button) has produced the block. Then call qapp.processEvents() to flush pending layout/paint events before screenshotting.',
