+  <li data-correct="false" data-why="The threshold does not absorb a changed digit. A different displayed number changes many pixels far beyond RMS 5. Freezing is required, not the threshold.">The threshold of 5 absorbs the small noise, so no fix is needed.</li>
+  <li data-correct="false" data-why="There is no random seed being set. The fix monkeypatches _get_reading to a constant; it does not seed the RNG.">A fixed random seed is set in conftest so <code>random.gauss</code> returns the same value each run.</li>
+  <li data-correct="false" data-why="The multimeter test is not skipped. It is made deterministic by freezing the reading, then it runs like any other block.">The multimeter test is skipped because noisy instruments can't be visually tested.</li>
